A||N||12||Seanh||Tires: 60 or 55 series???||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||06-12-2001||08:02 PM||||Help me out. I am getting new tires this week, front are currently 205/60R15 and rear 215/60R15's. I was thinking about changeing to 55 series on both ends, how big of a difference would this make. One thing I'm concerned about, I think cars will stock rims and little low pro tires and tons of wheel well showing look shitty, so I don't want this to happen with my car. So, I guess what I'm asking, how much smaller is the 55 series then the 60 series? Will it look goofy do you think, or even noticable? Which series do you think I should go with? Would the benefits of useing 55's be even noticable? Thanks for your input!||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||06-12-2001||08:21 PM||||If you want to see what 205 50 15 frt and <BR>215 60 15 back look like check out the Grand Bend <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008040.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008040.html</A> <P>The first black GT and the Copper GT both have this.  I like it.  If I were to change anything I would go 225 50 15 on the back<P><p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 06-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||06-12-2001||08:42 PM||||Hmm. So those cars have 50's on front and 60's on back? I can't really judge from the picts, but I think they look a little different then stock, don't you think? I don't think I really like that look. I don't know what to do! What advantages are there to doing 50's or 55's? 225's on the back ok? I was already thinking of doing that, but not sure.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||06-12-2001||08:47 PM||||Hey, how about doing either of these:<P>1) Dunlop SP Sport 5000 Asymmetrical:<BR>Fnt: 205/55R15<BR>Rear: 205/55R15<BR>(can I use the same size all around, any changes in handling, anything?)<P>2) Dunlop SP Sport 5000 Asymmetrical:<BR>Fnt: 205/50R15<BR>Rear: 215/50R15<P>How much smaller in overall dia. is a 50 series then a 60 series? I am think doing option 2 is the way to go, what do you think??? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||06-12-2001||09:01 PM||||Do 50 series look okay on stock rims? I think I'm goin with SP Sport 5000's 205/50R15 frnt and 215/50R15 in back. Whacha think???||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||06-12-2001||09:04 PM||||DONT PUT THE SAME SIZE TIRES ON THE FRT AS ON THE BACK.  IT WILL EFFECT HANDLING.<P>To wide on the frt and it gets harder to turn in a parking lot. <P>I like option number 2 But would maybe change your back to either<P>215 55 15 or **225 50 15** on the back.<P>I don't think 215 50 will be tall enough to fill those wheel openings correctly.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||06-12-2001||10:14 PM||||i have 205/60 16 fnt<BR>       225/60 16 rear<BR>just to fill out the wheel openings.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||06-12-2001||11:24 PM||||I got 225/50/15s all the way around one of my cars, not on stock rims though. I love the way it looks and it is not tough to drive in parking lots or at low speeds. The only thing that is bad is bumpsteer and hydroplaning. Any Fiero I have ever owned had these problems... I think it is a great size...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
Z||000008||Seanh||06-13-2001||12:38 AM||||Ok. I'm buying from <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com</A>  so I kinda have to go with what they have. What if I go with 205/50R15 on the fronts, and 225/60R15 on the back, they don't have the other 2 possibilites you meantioned. I could also jump up to 215/50R15 on the front, with 225/60R15 on back. Which would you reccomend?||||reg||1
Z||000009||ray b||06-13-2001||01:12 PM||||225-50-15 all round worked on my 87 se with 15-7 rims, speedo was spot on to.<BR>i put 50's on every car i ever owned. and wish i could go lower and wider like 195-45-15 front and 225-45-15 rear to lower the car<BR>without cut springs or f---ing up the suspension or ride<BR>btw tire rack has 195-45 -15 in koko or yoko brands but no biger sizes for rear yet.<BR>i can;t see tire gaps when in the car so i don't care bout that.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
